## 8. A Real-World DevOps Pipeline Example

Here's what happens when a developer pushes code:

```
1. Developer pushes code to GitHub/GitLab
            ↓
2. CI pipeline triggers automatically
            ↓
3. Code is compiled/built (npm build, maven build)
            ↓
4. Unit tests run (Jest, JUnit)
            ↓
5. Code quality scan (SonarQube)
            ↓
6. Security scan (Snyk, Trivy)
            ↓
7. Docker image is built
            ↓
8. Image is pushed to container registry (Docker Hub)
            ↓
9. Deploy to staging environment (Kubernetes)
            ↓
10. Integration/E2E tests run (Cypress, Selenium)
            ↓
11. Manual approval (or auto-deploy)
            ↓
12. Deploy to production (Kubernetes)
            ↓
13. Monitoring kicks in (Prometheus, Grafana)
            ↓
14. Alerts if anything goes wrong (PagerDuty, Slack)
```

### GitLab CI/CD Example:
```yaml
# .gitlab-ci.yml
stages:
  - build
  - test
  - security
  - deploy

build:
  stage: build
  script:
    - npm install
    - npm run build

test:
  stage: test
  script:
    - npm run test

security_scan:
  stage: security
  script:
    - trivy image my-app:latest

deploy_production:
  stage: deploy
  script:
    - kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yml
  only:
    - main
  when: manual
```

